        <workflow:AgenticOperation name="Copy A03 data into A04" status="Succeeded" captureOutput="true">
          <startedAt>2026-09-17T01:27:56</startedAt>
          <baseCommit>c1ef84c1e70a91fb58fc297f12881c9f89de11d2</baseCommit>
          <output>Task instructions for `A04_01_CopyData` executed:

1. **Wiped** the live `a04_rendering/data` tree (45 files) and removed it entirely.
2. **Copied** the full `a03_authoring/data` tree back in — same 45 files (1 DocSet, 9 PageGroups, 35 Pages), 1:1 path parity confirmed.
3. **Remapped** every file: package `a03_authoring.data` → `a04_rendering.data`, xmlns prefixes `a03data`/`a03pgroup` → `a04data`/`a04pgroup`, `BmlDocSet_A03` → `BmlDocSet_A04` (incl. file rename), and stray `a03`/`A03` prose tokens → `a04`/`A04`. The one special case — `BmlDocSet_A04.bml`'s provenance sentence, which named A03's own tasks (`A03_01_CopyData`/`A03_02_AuthorPages`) — was hand-rewritten to reference `A04_01_CopyData`/`A04_02_RenderPages` instead of a token swap, matching the established convention.
4. **Confirmed** no leftover `a03`/`A03`/cross-sector references remain in the imported tree (verified via grep), and pages/pageGroups/homePage/rootPageGroup lists resolve only to A04 Blocks.
5. **Catalog**: `Library.bml` already exports every current A04 data Block (same names as before) — no changes needed there.

Since A03's data content had changed since the last A04 build, this re-copy replaced the previously *rendered* A04 pages with fresh (unrendered) copies from A03 — 35 page files show as modified in `git status`; the 9 PageGroup files and the DocSet came out byte-identical to before. `npx blockml validate --all` shows no errors introduced in `a04_rendering/data` (the 5 pre-existing errors are unrelated, in historical `_meta/transform/succeeded` snapshot files referencing old task types).

The pipeline's next step, `A04_02_RenderPages`, is what will turn these copied pages back into rendered content — not part of this task.
</output>
